cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BOLA in the Wild: Taxonomy and Meta-Analysis of 100+ HackerOne Disclosures"
message: "If you use this dataset, taxonomy, or analysis framework in your research, please cite this repository."
type: dataset

authors:
  - family-names: "Kaur"
    given-names: "Bandana"
    affiliation: "APIsec Research Labs"

  - family-names: "Haro Peralta"
    given-names: "Jose"
    affiliation: "APIsec Research Labs"

abstract: >
  This repository accompanies the paper
  "Broken Object Level Authorization in the Wild:
  A Taxonomy and Quantitative Meta-Analysis of 100+ HackerOne Disclosures".
  It contains the manually verified dataset, taxonomy definitions,
  classifier prompts, and analysis scripts used to study real-world
  Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA) vulnerabilities disclosed
  through public bug bounty reports.

keywords:
  - API Security
  - BOLA
  - IDOR
  - Broken Object Level Authorization
  - Authorization
  - Bug Bounty
  - HackerOne
  - Application Security
  - Vulnerability Research
  - Taxonomy
  - Security Measurement

repository-code: "https://github.com/hackwither/bola-in-the-wild"

